course: dictionary
lesson: 5842
title: Names of places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names. Malacca is the name of one special place, so it starts with a capital letter, just like London or Glasgow. Read the words around it to see what kind of name it is. «Portugal seized the port of Malacca in 1511» tells you Malacca is a port, a place where ships load and unload.
explain: Look at «The Strait of Malacca is shown on maps of world trade routes.» A strait is a narrow stretch of sea between two pieces of land, so here Malacca names a sea passage. Always ask: is this a place, a thing or a person? The capital letter and the words near it give you the answer.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A malacca with a small m is a walking stick, but this meaning is rare. Check the sentence before you decide. «A malacca cane» means a stick, while «the port of Malacca» means a place.
fact: Malacca is a historic city and state in Malaysia, on the west coast of the Malay Peninsula.
fact: The Strait of Malacca is a narrow sea passage between Malaysia and the Indonesian island of Sumatra.
fact: Malacca was a famous old trading port where spices, silk and tea passed between many countries.
fact: Malacca is also spelled Melaka, so you may see either name on a map.
fact: A malacca (small m) is a walking stick made from a kind of rattan palm, and this meaning is rare.
exercise: «Portugal seized the port of Malacca in 1511.» What kind of word is Malacca here? | *A place name, with a capital letter | A type of ship | A colour of silk | A walking stick
exercise: «The Strait of Malacca is shown on maps of world trade routes.» What is the Strait of Malacca? | A walking stick made of rattan | A tall mountain in Malaysia | A city in Indonesia | *A narrow sea passage between Malaysia and Sumatra
exercise: Grandad walks slowly with «a malacca cane». What is a malacca here? | A city | *A walking stick | A sea | A ship
test: Why does Malacca start with a capital letter in «the port of Malacca»? | *Because it is the name of a particular place | Because it is in a list | Because it starts a sentence | Because it is a rare kind of stick
test: Which other spelling of Malacca is used on maps? | Maracas | *Melaka | Mamba | Mallorca
exam: Grandma says, «Malacca grew into one of Asia's greatest ports.» What does Malacca name here? | A type of silk | A rattan palm | A ship's captain | *A historic trading port
